# The reviewer's output contract (also the CLI's --json-schema): BLOCKs, each with a repro the verifier runs, and NOTEs for the human.
FINDINGS_SCHEMA='{"type":"object","properties":{"blocks":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"loc":{"type":"string"},"claim":{"type":"string"},"clause":{"type":"string"},"repro":{"type":"string"}},"required":["loc","claim","clause","repro"],"additionalProperties":false}},"notes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["blocks","notes"],"additionalProperties":false}'
# Egress. Every step runs on a per-run internal network (no route out, no external DNS) with its own proxy container on both that
# network and the bridge: proxy.js in this checkout, run in the sandbox image, CONNECT to the step's hosts on 443 and nothing else,
# one JSON line per decision into log.jsonl. The proxy vars are a courtesy to the clients: with no route out, a client that ignores
# them has no network, not an open one. Hosts are regex alternatives; the proxy anchors them (^(?:…)$) and refuses IP literals.
ALLOW_WORK='api\.anthropic\.com|registry\.npmjs\.org'   # Claude Code, and the repo's own installs
ALLOW_JUDGE='api\.openai\.com|registry\.npmjs\.org'     # Codex (its chatgpt.com model-list refresh is denied; non-fatal), and the repo's checks
ALLOW_PUSH='github\.com'
ALLOW_VERIFY='registry\.npmjs\.org'   # the verifier: the repo's own installs, nothing else; the review arm uses the worker's list
# The merge gate (docs/cascade-plan.md, option (c)): a task whose base_branch is NEXT_BRANCH is merged into it by the factory through its
# PR, when the verification gate passed, the chain base is already on next, the accumulation cap is not reached and the required checks
# are green, with a separate merger App's token minted for that step and held by no container. MERGER_APP_ID empty: PR-only mode (the
# gate opens PRs and stops). Set it by PR once the next ruleset and the App exist and `factory ruleset-check` and canary.sh pass on the mini.
